\import{fcap-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\tag{fcap}
\tag{spin}
\tag{representation-theory}

\taxon{Proposition}
\title{The outer nodes of #{D_4} permute the three eight-dimensional classes}

\p{Work over #{\mathbb C} with the type-#{D_4} Cartan and Borel of
\ref{fcap-002X}. In its orthonormal coordinates put

##{\begin{aligned}
\alpha_1&=\epsilon_1-\epsilon_2,&
\alpha_2&=\epsilon_2-\epsilon_3,\\
\alpha_3&=\epsilon_3-\epsilon_4,&
\alpha_4&=\epsilon_3+\epsilon_4.
\end{aligned}}

The central node is #{2}; the outer nodes are #{1,3,4}. Their fundamental
weights are

##{\omega_1=\epsilon_1,\qquad
\omega_3=\tfrac12(\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2+\epsilon_3-\epsilon_4),\qquad
\omega_4=\tfrac12(\epsilon_1+\epsilon_2+\epsilon_3+\epsilon_4).}

The established exterior convention identifies the vector class with
#{L(\omega_1)}, the all-plus half-spin class with
#{S^+=L(\omega_4)}, and the other half-spin class with
#{S^-=L(\omega_3)}; see \ref{fcap-002Y} and \ref{fcap-0030}. Each has
dimension eight.}

\p{Let #{\sigma} be any permutation of #{\{1,3,4\}}. The linear map
specified on the simple-root basis by

##{T_\sigma(\alpha_i)=\alpha_{\sigma(i)}\quad(i=1,3,4),\qquad
T_\sigma(\alpha_2)=\alpha_2}

preserves the #{D_4} Cartan matrix. Hence it is orthogonal, preserves the
root and coroot systems, and preserves the weight and coweight lattices.
It is therefore an automorphism of the simply connected based root datum.
Duality with the simple coroots gives

##{T_\sigma(\omega_i)=\omega_{\sigma(i)}\qquad(i=1,3,4).}

In particular an outer three-cycle has cube one and nontrivially cycles
the three labeled highest-weight classes

##{L(\omega_1),\qquad S^-=L(\omega_3),\qquad S^+=L(\omega_4).}

This is a permutation of based root data and of irreducible
highest-weight labels. A literal pullback of concrete group modules would
additionally require an actual group automorphism and a fixed direction;
that stronger statement is not inferred from this diagram calculation.}

\p{\citet{Section 20.3, pp. 312--314}{fulton2004representation}
give the same #{D_4} diagram and identify the vector and two half-spin
highest weights.
\citet{Chapter 5, Theorem 5.6, pp. 33--35}{adams1996exceptional}
independently identifies these as the three basic eight-dimensional
classes permuted by outer automorphisms. The first source is the complex
highest-weight comparison used here; Adams' theorem concerns the compact
actual group and is not being claimed as proved by the root-datum
calculation alone.}

\p{The pinned declaration
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.D4Tripled.trialityAutomorphism}
has cube one on a tripled type-#{D_4} toral-closure carrier and permutes
its numbered root and represented-torus coordinates. The inspected file
does not identify that carrier with standard #{\Spin_8}, prove its torus
maximal, or identify its three factors with the vector and half-spin
modules. It is precise formal context for the diagram symmetry, not a
whole-card formalization of the proposition above.}
